{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":296747,"duration_api_ms":296685,"num_turns":1,"result":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. Re-implementations diverge on edge cases. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI, and verifies parity through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: A four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify) with `cmd/` per-utility packages, `pkg/sys/` syscall abstractions, `pkg/format/` output formatting, `pkg/testutils/` differential testing harness, and `magefiles/` build targets. Specs live in `docs/`.\n\n**Current state**: Multiple utilities have specs complete (ts, wc, cat, sponge, du, ls). Generated code exists at `generation-merged` tags but not on the working branch. No code is present on the current branch.\n\n**Current release (04.0)**: \"Batch 4 — ls core specification and differential test.\" Use case `rel04.0-uc001-ls` has spec status `spec_complete` and code status `not started`. This is the target.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 04.0 has one use case: `rel04.0-uc001-ls` (ls core). The spec is complete — PRD, use case, and test suite all exist. Code generation has not run. The first task is the implementation of `cmd/ls/main.go` covering basic directory listing, entry filtering, sorting, and output formatting. Tests belong in a separate task (per P2). The implementation depends on `pkg/sys` and `pkg/format` (release 00.0), which may or may not exist on the working branch, so the task includes fallback guidance.\n\n## Proposed Tasks\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement ls core -- directory reading, filtering, sorting, and output (ls PRD)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (cmd/ component, pkg/sys/ component, pkg/format/ component, design decisions DD4 and DD6)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (locate the ls PRD -- the file matching *ls*.yaml in this directory)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel04.0-uc001-ls.yaml (ls core use case)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-04.0.yaml (ls core test suite)\n      - pkg/sys/ (review existing API for file metadata and terminal width if this package exists on the branch)\n      - pkg/format/ (review existing API for column alignment if this package exists on the branch)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/ls/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"Core ls implementation -- argument parsing, directory reading, entry filtering, sorting, output formatting\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Parse command-line arguments using the Go standard library flag package. Accept zero or more path operands. When no operands are given, default to listing the current directory.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Read directory contents using os.ReadDir for directory operands. For file operands, stat the file and include it directly. When multiple operands are given, list files first (sorted), then directories (sorted), each directory preceded by a 'dirname:' header line when more than one operand is present.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Filter entries by default to hide names starting with '.'. With -a, show all entries including '.' and '..'. With -A, show all entries except '.' and '..'.\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Sort entries by name in byte order (LC_ALL=C). Support -r to reverse any sort. Support -t to sort by modification time (newest first, break ties by name). Support -S to sort by file size (largest first, break ties by name).\"\n      - id: R5\n        text: \"When stdout is a terminal, output entries in multi-column format. When stdout is not a terminal, output one entry per line. -1 forces single-column output. -C forces multi-column output. Use pkg/format for column layout if available on the branch; otherwise implement minimal column logic with a default width of 80.\"\n      - id: R6\n        text: \"Exit 0 on success. Exit 2 if any operand cannot be accessed. Print errors to stderr in the GNU format: \\\"ls: cannot access '<path>': <error>\\\". Continue processing remaining operands after errors.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Use pkg/sys for terminal width detection and file metadata if the package exists on the current branch. If pkg/sys is not available, use os.Stat directly and default terminal width to 80 columns.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use pkg/format for multi-column layout if the package exists on the current branch. If pkg/format is not available, implement minimal column alignment using fixed-width string padding.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"All sorting uses byte-order comparison (LC_ALL=C semantics). Do not use locale-aware collation. This follows architecture design decision DD6.\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Detect whether stdout is a terminal using os.Stdout.Stat() and checking for os.ModeCharDevice. Do not add external dependencies beyond what is already in go.mod.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/ls/main.go exists and compiles with 'go build ./cmd/ls/'.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Running the binary with no arguments lists the current directory contents, hiding dotfiles, sorted alphabetically by byte order.\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"-a includes '.' and '..' entries. -A includes hidden entries except '.' and '..'.\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"-r reverses sort order. -t sorts by modification time (newest first). -S sorts by size (largest first). Ties are broken by name.\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Output is multi-column when stdout is a terminal; one-per-line when piped. -1 forces single-column. -C forces columns.\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"Non-existent or inaccessible paths produce GNU-format errors on stderr and exit code 2 without stopping remaining operands.\"\n```","stop_reason":null,"session_id":"e4e27ed5-4c55-42c0-9e30-c5797cc8dab0","total_cost_usd":0.506403,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15824,"cache_read_input_tokens":19286,"output_tokens":15914,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":15824},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":15914,"cacheReadInputTokens":19286,"cacheCreationInputTokens":15824,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.506403,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"uuid":"cbb0e2b6-ffd5-433c-8d2c-5437cabf60c9"}
